        "original_id": "a0d04e2a-db39-53e8-9ed2-2c5731104f3e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenji Satake, Brian Atwater, David Yamaguchi\n- Events: 1700 Cascadia earthquake, Japanese orphan tsunami\n- Places: Cascadia subduction zone, Japan\n- Concepts: tsunami origin research, moment magnitude\n\nFacts:\n- On January 26, 1700, the 1700 Cascadia earthquake occurred along the Cascadia subduction zone.\n- The 1700 Cascadia earthquake had an estimated moment magnitude of 8.7 to 9.2.\n- Kenji Satake, Brian Atwater, and David Yamaguchi assembled disparate pieces of information about a Japanese tsunami that had no known origin.",
